IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sgia-p1-definitions`
IMPORT `ma-nouns`

-- Misrepresentation Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation
-- LAYER 1, THE ACT'S WORDS AS THE INTERPRETATION ACT 1965 DEFINES THEM.
--
-- The Act defines no term of its own.  Two of its words are defined by the Interpretation Act 1965
-- s 2(1): "person" and "party" (the Act speaks of "a person" in ss 1 to 3 and "a party" in ss 2 and 3),
-- and "court" (s 2(2)).  This module looks both up in the table of that Act's s 2(1), which is
-- copied unchanged from Commons (sgia-p1-definitions.l4; see NOTES.md, Dependencies).
-- Nothing in ss 1 to 4 calls this module: the rules there take "a person has entered into a
-- contract" and "the court or arbitrator" as facts.  The seat asks the two questions below on their own.
--
-- Reading a result.  The Interpretation Act says "person" and "party" INCLUDE a company, an
-- association and a body of persons, so the list is not closed: a thing it does not name (an individual,
-- whose status rests on the ordinary meaning of "person", or anything else) answers NOTHING.
-- It says "court" MEANS any court of competent jurisdiction in Singapore, so a body that is not
-- such a court answers JUST FALSE.

§ `The Act's words, as the Interpretation Act 1965 s 2(1) defines them`

-- src:34 | 1. Where a person has entered into a contract after a
-- src:35 | misrepresentation has been made to him, and —
@ref ss 1 to 3 "a person" and "a party", with Interpretation Act 1965 s 2(1) "person"; "party" (src:34-35)
GIVEN party IS A `Kind of party`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 1 to 3 "person" and "party" include the party (Interpretation Act s 2(1))` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the definition of` "person"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Interpretation Act's table has no entry for "person"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST d THEN
        BRANCH
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Interpretation Act's entry is not an "includes" definition
            IF NOT (d's kind EQUALS Includes) THEN NOTHING
            -- the entry names "any company"
            IF party EQUALS `A company` AND elem "any company" (d's `what the Act names`) THEN JUST TRUE
            -- the entry names "association"
            IF party EQUALS `An association` AND elem "association" (d's `what the Act names`) THEN JUST TRUE
            -- the entry names "body of persons"
            IF party EQUALS `Another body of persons` AND elem "body of persons" (d's `what the Act names`) THEN JUST TRUE
            -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "include" adds to the ordinary meaning and names no individual; an individual's status rests on the ordinary meaning, which the Act does not state
            IF party EQUALS `An individual` THEN NOTHING
            -- NOTHING-kind (includes): the list after "include" is not closed, and this kind of party is not in it
            OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:68 | be or has been rescinded, the court or arbitrator may declare the
@ref s 2(2) "the court", with Interpretation Act 1965 s 2(1) "court" (src:68-68)
GIVEN body IS A `Body asked about`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(2) the body is a "court" (Interpretation Act s 2(1))` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the definition of` "court"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Interpretation Act's table has no entry for "court"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST d THEN
        BRANCH
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Interpretation Act's entry is not a "means" definition
            IF NOT (d's kind EQUALS Means) THEN NOTHING
            IF body EQUALS `A court of competent jurisdiction in Singapore` AND elem "any court of competent jurisdiction in Singapore" (d's `what the Act names`) THEN JUST TRUE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "\"court\" means any court of competent jurisdiction in Singapore" (Interpretation Act 1965 s 2(1)); this body is not one
            IF body EQUALS `Any other court` THEN JUST FALSE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "\"court\" means any court of competent jurisdiction in Singapore" (Interpretation Act 1965 s 2(1)); this body is not a court
            IF body EQUALS `Any other body` THEN JUST FALSE
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Interpretation Act's entry does not name a court of competent jurisdiction in Singapore
            OTHERWISE NOTHING
